\value{
The estimators return the estimate over the event times with its
standard error and confidence band; \code{morie_cox_ph} returns
coefficients with standard errors, hazard ratios and the
likelihood-ratio test; \code{morie_concordance_index} returns the
C-index with its pair counts.
}
\description{
Kaplan-Meier and Nelson-Aalen estimation, the log-rank test, Cox
proportional-hazards regression with Efron tie handling, and Harrell's
concordance index.
}
\details{
Verified against R's \pkg{survival} package.  Note
\code{survival::survfit}'s \code{std.err} is the standard error of the
CUMULATIVE HAZARD; this returns both, as \code{se_cumhaz} and
\code{se}, which differ by a factor of \eqn{S(t)}.  Censoring is
handled explicitly throughout: a subject still at risk at the end of
follow-up contributes the information that it survived that long, and
treating it either as an event or as absent biases every estimate.  The
same functions exist in the Python package as
\code{morie.fn._survival_core}.
}
